      "report_date": "2026-11-26",
      "title": "182 Banks, 38 Crypto Platforms, One Toolkit: The Godfather Tech Android Fraud Arsenal",
      "summary": "The Godfather Tech seller, using the Telegram name 教父科技, offers Android remote-access trojans, source code and fraud-related setup services, largely built on the Flying Eagle RAT codebase resold under several brand names. The toolkit combines remote control, keylogging, screen overlays and camera access, and its builder produces apps that are repackaged, signed and tuned to survive on major Android phone brands. Operators can push fake bank and crypto login screens over legitimate apps to capture credentials, payment PINs and wallet recovery words, then read SMS codes and move money remotely. The fake-screen catalogues list 182 banks and 38 crypto platforms that the kit was configured to impersonate, which the report notes does not confirm any breach. For defenders, the shared code, class names and panel paths help link related copies, and the report recommends monitoring for combined Accessibility, device-admin and SMS permissions.",
      "completeness": "High",
